<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 323.1 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 323.1 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of December 12 raised 323.1 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 468.7 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 138 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    13.86 (14.36)	   47.2 (86.9)</p>
<p>    Six months		15.13 (16.48)	   71.7 (58.9)</p>
<p>    12 months		 14.80 (17.50)	   78.8 (57.5)</p>
<p>    24 months		 20.50 (20.76)	  125.4 (265.4)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,552.75 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,553.5 a week earlier and 1,598 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
